window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-be80d2db315aa944"]={"key":"ny_b1-be80d2db315aa944","group":"ny_b1","uid":"be80d2db315aa944","rank":100,"title":"duncastle interview travel sequence plan","occupation":"private_detectives_investigators","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You are Solomon Ngata, the investigator supporting Duncastle Wholesale’s employee-interview file. Freya Lindholm in HR needs a written plan she can use to staff and brief the six retail branches and two depots before the external auditors take the completed file at close of business on 11 December. You have authorization for thirty-one employee interviews, and the schedule needs to show the dated sequence, travel between locations, dependencies, and who is needed at each session. The planning picture is awkward: three depot interviews only make sense after the relevant goods-in supervisors have been seen; employees at a branch tend to hear about interviews within a day, which may affect the order and the way sessions are described; one branch trades only Thursday through Sunday; and two sites are four hours apart. Freya cannot attend two locations at once, although the people responsible for a session may differ by location. There is no second HR partner available, and the working window is too tight to use an ideal fully witnessed sequence for every session, so make any fallback visible and defensible rather than quietly implying that the constraint does not exist. Freya has also informally promised the audit contact that the file will show every interview arranged before the handover, even where the final appointment depends on local confirmation; do not turn that promise into a claim that attendance or evidence is guaranteed. Prepare `duncastle_interview_travel_sequence_plan.docx` and write it into the top level of the working directory you start in, using exactly that filename. Keep it to no more than four pages. It is for people who were not in the planning conversation, so include a compact orientation or legend, make the dates, sites, participants, travel assumptions, dependencies, open confirmations, and fallback legible, and distinguish a planned booking from a completed interview. Do not recommend investigative findings or take action on anyone’s behalf; present only the operational plan and its limits, and do not add interviews, sites, or people beyond the authorized scope.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `duncastle_interview_travel_sequence_plan.docx` — A concise, dated interview and travel sequencing plan for the authorized employee interviews, suitable for HR staffing and external-audit handover. (Top-level working-directory filename must match exactly. Maximum four pages. Must cover all 31 authorized interviews across six branches and two depots, show sequence, dates, locations, required participants, travel, dependencies, confirmations, status distinctions, and any fallback without inventing extra scope or claiming completed evidence.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/duncastle_interview_travel_sequence_plan.docx","bytes":41788,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/f2d6e07f356ed5140fe344eede3ab27cc6fb60d30a1fbec50e3f3c63e896abc9.docx","sha256":"f2d6e07f356ed5140fe344eede3ab27cc6fb60d30a1fbec50e3f3c63e896abc9","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"DUNCASTLE WHOLESALE\nEmployee Interview Travel Sequence Plan\nOperational plan for HR staffing and external-audit file handover | Window: 01-11 December 2026 | Handover: close of business, 11 December\nOrientation and control notes\nControl\nMeaning\nPurpose\n31 authorized employee-interview appointments across six branches and two depots. Prepared by investigator Solomon Ngata for HR partner Freya Lindholm and site coordinators. This is an operational booking plan only: no findings, attendance, evidence, or interview completion is asserted.\nStatus / confirmation\nBOOKED = calendar slot arranged; PLANNED = intended slot with local confirmation open; RESERVED = travel time, not an interview. No row is marked completed. The audit commitment is to show every appointment arranged before handover, including planned appointments; it does not guarantee attendance or evidence.\nStaffing\nSolomon is required for every interview. Freya is the sole HR partner and is scheduled only once at any time. Where F1 appears, the labeled fallback is Solomon plus the named site coordinator as local witness; the coordinator confirms room, attendee and witness record before the slot. Limitation: this is not the ideal Freya-attended arrangement.\nDependency gates\nD1-01 follows B1-01 (Northgate goods-in supervisor); D1-02 follows B2-01 (Riverway goods-in supervisor); D2-01 follows B3-01 (Meadow Park goods-in supervisor). “Gate” means do not start the depot session unless its prerequisite interview has been conducted; retain the booking as pending if it has not.\nSequence / travel\nBranch information may circulate within one day. The plan therefore batches each branch in a single morning, then moves to the next site; this is a neutral scheduling limitation, not a conclusion about staff. Meadow Park Branch trades Thursday-Sunday only. Meadow Park and West Distribution Depot are approximately four hours apart; T-01 reserves the driving leg and 30-minute contingency.\nLocation allocation\nLocation\nType / availability\nAuthorized interviews\nNorthgate Branch\nBranch\n4\nRiverway Branch\nBranch\n4\nMeadow Park Branch\nBranch - Thursday-Sunday trading only\n4\nHarbour Branch\nBranch\n4\nEastfield Branch\nBranch\n4\nHilltop Branch\nBranch\n4\nCentral Distribution Depot\nDepot\n4\nWest Distribution Depot\nDepot\n3\nTotal authorized interviews\n\n31\nBooking owner convention: each “Open” confirmation is owned by the specified site coordinator. Travel estimates and room availability remain planning assumptions until locally confirmed.\n\n\nDated operational schedule | 01-03 December\nSeq / ID\nDate / time\n(local)\nSite\nInterviewee role\nRequired staffing\nStatus / confirmation\nDependency or timing note\n01 / B1-01\n01 Dec\nTue\n08:30-09:15\nNorthgate Branch (Branch)\nGoods-in supervisor\nSolomon + Freya\nBOOKED\n-\nB1-01 prerequisite for D1-01\n02 / B1-02\n01 Dec\nTue\n09:30-10:15\nNorthgate Branch (Branch)\nBranch manager\nSolomon + Freya\nBOOKED\n-\nsame-site buffer 15m\n03 / B1-03\n01 Dec\nTue\n10:30-11:15\nNorthgate Branch (Branch)\nSales-floor colleague\nSolomon + Freya\nBOOKED\n-\nsame-site buffer 15m\n04 / B1-04\n01 Dec\nTue\n11:30-12:15\nNorthgate Branch (Branch)\nCash-office colleague\nSolomon + Freya\nPLANNED\nOpen: Northgate site coordinator\nlocal confirmation due before slot\n05 / B2-01\n02 Dec\nWed\n08:30-09:15\nRiverway Branch (Branch)\nGoods-in supervisor\nSolomon + Freya\nBOOKED\n-\nB2-01 prerequisite for D1-02\n06 / B2-02\n02 Dec\nWed\n09:30-10:15\nRiverway Branch (Branch)\nBranch manager\nSolomon + Freya\nBOOKED\n-\nsame-site buffer 15m\n07 / B2-03\n02 Dec\nWed\n10:30-11:15\nRiverway Branch (Branch)\nStock-control colleague\nSolomon + Freya\nPLANNED\nOpen: Riverway site coordinator\nlocal confirmation due before slot\n08 / B2-04\n02 Dec\nWed\n11:30-12:15\nRiverway Branch (Branch)\nCheckout colleague\nSolomon + Freya\nBOOKED\n-\nsame-site buffer 15m\n09 / B3-01\n03 Dec\nThu\n08:30-09:15\nMeadow Park Branch (Branch)\nGoods-in supervisor\nSolomon + Freya\nBOOKED\n-\nB3-01 prerequisite for D2-01\n10 / B3-02\n03 Dec\nThu\n09:30-10:15\nMeadow Park Branch (Branch)\nBranch manager\nSolomon + Freya\nBOOKED\n-\nrestricted branch: Thu-Sun\n11 / B3-03\n03 Dec\nThu\n10:30-11:15\nMeadow Park Branch (Branch)\nStockroom colleague\nSolomon + Freya\nPLANNED\nOpen: Meadow Park site coordinator\nrestricted branch: Thu-Sun\nTiming convention: all times are local site time. Each 45-minute appointment is separated by a 15-minute same-site buffer. No interview is a completed interview until attendance and record closure are separately logged.\n\n\nDated operational schedule | 03-06 December\nSeq / ID\nDate / time\n(local)\nSite\nInterviewee role\nRequired staffing\nStatus / confirmation\nDependency or timing note\nT-01\n04 Dec Fri\n08:00-12:00\nTRAVEL\nMeadow Park -> West Depot\nNot an interview\nSolomon + Freya\nRESERVED\n4h driving estimate + 30m contingency; next session 13:00\n12 / B3-04\n03 Dec\nThu\n11:30-12:15\nMeadow Park Branch (Branch)\nSales-floor colleague\nSolomon + Freya\nBOOKED\n-\nrestricted branch: Thu-Sun\n13 / D2-01\n04 Dec\nFri\n13:00-13:45\nWest Distribution Depot (Depot)\nDepot goods-in records colleague\nSolomon + Freya\nBOOKED\nGate: B3-01 conducted first\nafter T-01; do not start if gate unmet\n14 / D2-02\n04 Dec\nFri\n14:00-14:45\nWest Distribution Depot (Depot)\nDepot shift colleague\nSolomon + local site coordinator\nPLANNED\nOpen: West Depot site coordinator\nFALLBACK F1; local witness record\n15 / D2-03\n04 Dec\nFri\n15:00-15:45\nWest Distribution Depot (Depot)\nDepot dispatch colleague\nSolomon + local site coordinator\nPLANNED\nOpen: West Depot site coordinator\nFALLBACK F1; local witness record\n16 / D1-01\n05 Dec\nSat\n08:30-09:15\nCentral Distribution Depot (Depot)\nDepot goods-in records colleague\nSolomon + Freya\nBOOKED\nGate: B1-01 conducted first\ndependent depot appointment\n17 / D1-02\n05 Dec\nSat\n09:30-10:15\nCentral Distribution Depot (Depot)\nDepot receiving colleague\nSolomon + Freya\nBOOKED\nGate: B2-01 conducted first\ndependent depot appointment\n18 / D1-03\n05 Dec\nSat\n10:30-11:15\nCentral Distribution Depot (Depot)\nDepot inventory colleague\nSolomon + local site coordinator\nPLANNED\nOpen: Central Depot site coordinator\nFALLBACK F1; local witness record\n19 / D1-04\n05 Dec\nSat\n11:30-12:15\nCentral Distribution Depot (Depot)\nDepot administration colleague\nSolomon + local site coordinator\nPLANNED\nOpen: Central Depot site coordinator\nFALLBACK F1; local witness record\n20 / B4-01\n06 Dec\nSun\n08:30-09:15\nHarbour Branch (Branch)\nGoods-in colleague\nSolomon + Freya\nBOOKED\n-\nsame-site buffer 15m\n21 / B4-02\n06 Dec\nSun\n09:30-10:15\nHarbour Branch (Branch)\nBranch manager\nSolomon + Freya\nBOOKED\n-\nsame-site buffer 15m\nTiming convention: all times are local site time. Each 45-minute appointment is separated by a 15-minute same-site buffer. No interview is a completed interview until attendance and record closure are separately logged.\n\n\nDated operational schedule | 06-08 December and handover\nSeq / ID\nDate / time\n(local)\nSite\nInterviewee role\nRequired staffing\nStatus / confirmation\nDependency or timing note\n22 / B4-03\n06 Dec\nSun\n10:30-11:15\nHarbour Branch (Branch)\nCustomer-service colleague\nSolomon + local site coordinator\nPLANNED\nOpen: Harbour site coordinator\nFALLBACK F1; local witness record\n23 / B4-04\n06 Dec\nSun\n11:30-12:15\nHarbour Branch (Branch)\nCash-office colleague\nSolomon + local site coordinator\nPLANNED\nOpen: Harbour site coordinator\nFALLBACK F1; local witness record\n24 / B5-01\n07 Dec\nMon\n08:30-09:15\nEastfield Branch (Branch)\nGoods-in colleague\nSolomon + Freya\nBOOKED\n-\nsame-site buffer 15m\n25 / B5-02\n07 Dec\nMon\n09:30-10:15\nEastfield Branch (Branch)\nBranch manager\nSolomon + Freya\nBOOKED\n-\nsame-site buffer 15m\n26 / B5-03\n07 Dec\nMon\n10:30-11:15\nEastfield Branch (Branch)\nStock-control colleague\nSolomon + Freya\nPLANNED\nOpen: Eastfield site coordinator\nlocal confirmation due before slot\n27 / B5-04\n07 Dec\nMon\n11:30-12:15\nEastfield Branch (Branch)\nSales-floor colleague\nSolomon + Freya\nBOOKED\n-\nsame-site buffer 15m\n28 / B6-01\n08 Dec\nTue\n08:30-09:15\nHilltop Branch (Branch)\nGoods-in colleague\nSolomon + Freya\nBOOKED\n-\nsame-site buffer 15m\n29 / B6-02\n08 Dec\nTue\n09:30-10:15\nHilltop Branch (Branch)\nBranch manager\nSolomon + Freya\nBOOKED\n-\nsame-site buffer 15m\n30 / B6-03\n08 Dec\nTue\n10:30-11:15\nHilltop Branch (Branch)\nStockroom colleague\nSolomon + local site coordinator\nPLANNED\nOpen: Hilltop site coordinator\nFALLBACK F1; local witness record\n31 / B6-04\n08 Dec\nTue\n11:30-12:15\nHilltop Branch (Branch)\nCheckout colleague\nSolomon + Freya\nPLANNED\nOpen: Hilltop site coordinator\nfinal scheduled interview; before 11 Dec handover\nTiming convention: all times are local site time. Each 45-minute appointment is separated by a 15-minute same-site buffer. No interview is a completed interview until attendance and record closure are separately logged.\nHandover boundary\nFinal scheduled interview: B6-04, 08 Dec 2026, 11:30-12:15, Hilltop Branch, status PLANNED (local confirmation open). The operational deadline is external-audit file handover at close of business on 11 Dec 2026. That handover is separate from interview attendance or record completion.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The plan accounts for exactly 31 authorized employee interviews.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Interview schedule and any stated totals","grader_hint":"Count distinct scheduled interview entries or clearly identified sessions; accept grouped entries only when each of the 31 interviews remains individually traceable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The plan covers six retail branches and two depots, with each location identifiable.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Site field, site summary, or location legend","grader_hint":"Verify eight distinct sites and that the six branches and two depots are distinguishable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies Duncastle Wholesale, Solomon Ngata, and Freya Lindholm in their operational roles.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Title, orientation, or schedule legend","grader_hint":"Check names and roles directly in the rendered document."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document is no more than four pages when rendered.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered page count","grader_hint":"Render the DOCX with an offline office suite and count pages."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The required DOCX exists at the exact top-level filename requested.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Filesystem and document properties","grader_hint":"Check exact path and extension; this is a scaffolding item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every interview entry has a date or explicitly dated date range.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Schedule rows","grader_hint":"No interview may be left temporally unplaced."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every interview entry has a location and location type.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Schedule rows","grader_hint":"Verify branch/depot classification is present or unambiguously defined by the legend."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every interview entry identifies the employee or role being interviewed without inventing unsupported personal identities.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Interviewee field","grader_hint":"Accept role-level labels where names are unavailable; reject fabricated employee names presented as facts."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every session identifies who must be present or needed to staff it, including the investigator and any HR or local role dependency.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Participants/staffing field","grader_hint":"Check each row rather than accepting a generic statement that staffing is required."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The plan distinguishes a planned booking from a completed interview.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Status legend and row status","grader_hint":"Look for explicit status vocabulary and ensure scheduled sessions are not marked completed merely because they are listed."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The sequence is ordered chronologically and remains readable when followed from the first to last session.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Dates, times, sequence numbers","grader_hint":"Check ordering across all schedule sections, not just within a site."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The schedule identifies the handover deadline of 11 December and places the authorized work before or at that deadline.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Timeline and deadline note","grader_hint":"Verify the closing date is explicit and no planned session is silently placed after it."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Three depot interviews are explicitly linked to completion of the relevant goods-in-supervisor interviews.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Dependency column or dependency map","grader_hint":"Identify all three depot entries and verify each has a named prerequisite relationship."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The prerequisites for the depot interviews are scheduled earlier than their dependent depot interviews.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Dates and dependency references","grader_hint":"Compare the dates of each goods-in-supervisor prerequisite and dependent depot session."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The plan identifies which goods-in supervisor interview supports each depot dependency rather than treating all prerequisites as interchangeable.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-reference IDs or explicit dependency text","grader_hint":"Require traceable one-to-one or otherwise explicit mapping for all three depot dependencies."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Thursday-to-Sunday-only branch is identified and every session assigned there falls within those trading days.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Site availability note and dates","grader_hint":"Determine the restricted branch from the document and check every assigned date against Thursday through Sunday."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The plan states the four-hour travel relationship between the two distant sites.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Travel assumptions or route notes","grader_hint":"The relationship may be expressed as approximately four hours; it must identify both sites."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The schedule does not place the investigator in sessions at the two four-hour-apart sites without accounting for the travel leg.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Daily sequence and travel blocks","grader_hint":"Check same-day transitions and next-day placement; a bare back-to-back crossing fails."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Travel time is separated from interview time or otherwise visibly reserved in the schedule.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Calendar blocks, travel column, or timing convention","grader_hint":"A narrative assumption alone is insufficient if the schedule implies simultaneous travel and interviewing."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Freya Lindholm is never scheduled at two locations at the same time.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Participant assignments and timestamps","grader_hint":"Compare all rows involving Freya for overlapping times and locations."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The plan states how sessions not attended by Freya are staffed or what confirmation remains open.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Staffing/fallback notes","grader_hint":"Require a named responsible role or an explicit unresolved confirmation, not an unexplained omission."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The plan identifies the one-HR-partner constraint as a planning assumption or limitation.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Orientation or limitations note","grader_hint":"Check that the constraint is visible to downstream users."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The schedule shows a defensible fallback for the sessions that cannot use the ideal fully witnessed arrangement.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Fallback/exception field","grader_hint":"Accept a clearly labeled alternative staffing or sequencing arrangement with its limitation; do not require one particular method."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The fallback is operationally usable rather than a vague instruction to resolve the conflict later.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Fallback description and affected rows","grader_hint":"Judge whether HR could understand who covers the session, what remains to confirm, and how the exception is recorded."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The plan marks open local confirmations separately from booked or completed status.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Status/confirmation fields","grader_hint":"Look for explicit labels such as pending confirmation, provisional, booked, or completed."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The informal promise to show every interview arranged before handover is represented as a planning commitment, not evidence that all attendance is guaranteed.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope or limitations note","grader_hint":"Verify the distinction between arranged and attended/completed."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document communicates the schedule’s limits without undermining its usefulness for staffing.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered document as a whole","grader_hint":"A professional reader should be able to tell what is actionable, what is provisional, and what is not asserted."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The plan accounts for the risk that branch information travels within one day through sequencing, spacing, or an explicit risk note.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Sequence rationale or operational note","grader_hint":"Require a visible treatment of the one-day information-spread fact, not merely repetition of it."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The treatment of information spread is neutral and operational, without alleging misconduct or directing investigative action.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Narrative notes and labels","grader_hint":"Reject speculative conclusions about employees; accept a neutral scheduling or confidentiality limitation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The plan gives enough timing detail to identify daily order and travel feasibility.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Start/end times, blocks, or explicit daily order","grader_hint":"A date-only list fails unless the document clearly defines a feasible daily sequencing convention."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"No person is assigned to overlapping interviews or travel blocks.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All time and participant assignments","grader_hint":"Check Solomon, Freya, and any named or role-based staff for collisions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The schedule includes a reasonable buffer or explicit contingency treatment for travel and appointment slippage.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Travel blocks, buffer notation, or contingency note","grader_hint":"Judge against the four-hour route and multi-day deadline; do not demand a particular buffer length."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document makes clear whether dates and times are local to the sites or uses one consistent time convention.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Legend or schedule header","grader_hint":"Accept a single-site jurisdiction if explicitly stated; ambiguity across locations fails."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each depot is distinguishable from the branches in the schedule and summary.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Location labels and legend","grader_hint":"Check that depot-specific dependencies can be found without inference."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The plan identifies the relevant goods-in supervisors as roles rather than silently treating depot interviews as independent.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Dependency rows or staffing notes","grader_hint":"The role must be visible wherever it is a prerequisite."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The schedule provides a unique identifier or equivalent traceable label for each interview.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Interview IDs, row numbers, or unambiguous composite labels","grader_hint":"Verify that dependencies and status references point to unique entries."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document includes a compact legend explaining its status, participant, dependency, and travel notation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Legend/orientation block","grader_hint":"The legend need not use exact words, but a new reader must understand the symbols and fields."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"A downstream HR coordinator who was not part of the planning conversation can use the document without asking the author what the rows mean.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered document as a whole","grader_hint":"Judge independent usability, especially traceability from a session to its staffing and travel requirements."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The plan identifies the external-audit handover as the operational deadline and does not confuse it with interview completion status.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Deadline and status language","grader_hint":"Check for explicit distinction between file handover and evidence completion."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The plan states the scope as employee interviews and does not expand it into findings, disciplinary decisions, or recommendations.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope statement and content","grader_hint":"Check the document’s stated purpose and substantive content."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The schedule is presented as a professional report that can be handed to HR and an external auditor without extensive reformatting.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered document","grader_hint":"Assess hierarchy, legibility, consistent labels, and whether operational information is easy to locate."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The plan provides a location-level summary allowing a reader to see how many authorized interviews are assigned to each of the eight sites.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Summary table or countable schedule","grader_hint":"Counts must reconcile to the 31 interview entries; a reader may calculate them if site labels are consistent."},{"rubric_item_id":"R43","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The plan provides a date-level or day-level view sufficient to see the operational load and sequence.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Calendar view, daily grouping, or date column","grader_hint":"The main schedule may satisfy this if daily grouping is genuinely readable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R44","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The schedule identifies any same-site batching or consecutive sessions in a way that does not imply simultaneous interviews.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Times and sequence labels","grader_hint":"Check that batching remains sequential and resource-feasible."},{"rubric_item_id":"R45","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The plan does not place a session at the restricted branch outside its stated Thursday-to-Sunday operating window.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Dates and branch availability","grader_hint":"Independent check of every row at that branch."},{"rubric_item_id":"R46","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The four-hour travel relationship is reflected in the ordering or in a clearly labeled non-driving alternative/contingency.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Route sequence and travel notes","grader_hint":"The document must show how the fact affects the plan, not merely mention four hours."},{"rubric_item_id":"R47","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The plan states which travel assumptions are estimates or require confirmation.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Assumptions/limitations note","grader_hint":"Look for an explicit boundary between planning assumptions and confirmed arrangements."},{"rubric_item_id":"R48","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The plan names the responsible party or role for confirming each open appointment or site dependency.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Owner/confirmation field","grader_hint":"A generic 'confirm locally' without an owner does not satisfy this."},{"rubric_item_id":"R49","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document includes a clear way to identify the next scheduled session after any travel or dependency block.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Sequence IDs, arrows, or chronological table","grader_hint":"A reader should not have to reconstruct order from scattered prose."},{"rubric_item_id":"R50","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The layout remains readable at normal viewing or print scale despite containing 31 interviews and travel information.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered pages","grader_hint":"Penalize microscopic text, clipped cells, excessive crossing lines, or unreadable dense tables."},{"rubric_item_id":"R51","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"All named participants in the schedule are limited to Solomon Ngata, Freya Lindholm, or clearly labeled workplace roles; no unsupported named personnel are introduced.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Names and staffing fields","grader_hint":"Role labels such as goods-in supervisor or site coordinator are acceptable; fabricated personal names are not."},{"rubric_item_id":"R52","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The plan uses a consistent site naming scheme across schedule, travel notes, dependencies, and summary.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-document internal consistency","grader_hint":"Minor abbreviations are acceptable only when defined in the legend."},{"rubric_item_id":"R53","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The plan identifies the final scheduled interview and its relationship to the 11 December handover without asserting that it has already occurred.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Final schedule entry and status","grader_hint":"Check both chronological placement and status wording."},{"rubric_item_id":"R54","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The artifact makes one deliberate, coherent sequencing choice where the brief permits two defensible readings, and signals the governing consideration rather than presenting an accidental order.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Sequence rationale, assumptions, or visible ordering","grader_hint":"Accept either defensible interpretation of the information-spread and dependency tension if chosen consistently and made legible."},{"rubric_item_id":"R55","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The artifact does not end with an unbounded next-steps list or a recommendation; it ends with the operational plan, its status, or its stated limitation.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Final page and closing text","grader_hint":"A concise confirmation note is acceptable; recommendations or investigative conclusions are not."},{"rubric_item_id":"R56","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The plan schedules or implies more than the 31 authorized interviews, adds unauthorized sites, or invents an additional interview category.","weight":-5.0,"polarity":"penalty","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Entire schedule and scope statements","grader_hint":"Apply once for any over-production beyond the six branches, two depots, and 31 authorized employee interviews; do not penalize neutral explanatory labels."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Duncastle Wholesale is preparing an employee-interview file for external auditors. Investigator Solomon Ngata must package a clear operational schedule for HR partner Freya Lindholm and downstream site coordinators before the file closes.","difficulty_sources":["sequencing a finite set of interviews around site availability, travel time, dependencies, information-spread risk, and a single HR partner","presenting an explicit and operationally usable plan without adding unsupported interview subjects or site categories","choosing and stating a defensible fallback when the available staffing and travel time make an ideal sequence impractical","handling an informal delivery promise without presenting an unsupported certainty"],"authoring_plan":{"purpose":"Build a synthetic but internally consistent gold DOCX showing an instructional, operational interview-and-travel sequencing plan for Duncastle Wholesale. No reference files are supplied; all facts needed for the gold are derived from the request and occupational practice.","content_constraints":["Create exactly 31 traceable interview entries across exactly six retail branches and two depots.","Use Solomon Ngata and Freya Lindholm as the only named people in the artifact; use role labels for employees, goods-in supervisors, and local site staff unless a supplied name exists.","Choose dates before or on 11 December and define a consistent time convention. Make the restricted branch’s entries Thursday through Sunday only.","Create three explicit depot-to-goods-in-supervisor dependencies and schedule each prerequisite before its depot interview.","Choose two sites as the four-hour-apart pair, state that relationship, and make travel blocks or day separation reflect it.","Ensure Freya never overlaps herself. Include the one-HR-partner constraint and a concrete, labeled fallback for sessions that cannot use ideal HR attendance.","Make the information-spread issue visible through a coherent sequencing choice or neutral operational limitation. Do not infer wrongdoing or investigative findings.","Represent Freya’s informal promise as a commitment to show arrangements before handover, while distinguishing planned, pending, booked, and completed statuses and avoiding guarantees.","Include an orientation/legend, schedule, travel/assumptions treatment, dependencies, open confirmations, and a concise limitations or fallback note. Keep the rendered document within four pages.","Do not add extra interviews, sites, unauthorized categories, recommendations, disciplinary outcomes, or claims that interviews or evidence are complete merely because they are scheduled."],"gold_derivation":"Construct a plausible schedule in Python or a spreadsheet-like data structure with 31 unique IDs, site type, role-level interviewee, date, start/end, participants, status, dependency, and travel fields. Validate programmatically that counts equal 31, there are eight sites, restricted-branch dates are Thursday-Sunday, all three depot prerequisites precede dependents, no participant overlaps, and the four-hour route is accounted for. Render to DOCX using standard office tooling, then inspect page count and readability. The gold can select any defensible ordering for the one permitted ambiguity, provided the rationale or limitation is explicit. Evaluate the penalty by checking scope counts and site/category labels rather than by matching exact values."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"mixed_media_bundle","structure":"freeform"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"interview_travel_plan","filename":"duncastle_interview_travel_sequence_plan.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A concise, dated interview and travel sequencing plan for the authorized employee interviews, suitable for HR staffing and external-audit handover.","required":true,"constraints":["Top-level working-directory filename must match exactly. Maximum four pages. Must cover all 31 authorized interviews across six branches and two depots, show sequence, dates, locations, required participants, travel, dependencies, confirmations, status distinctions, and any fallback without inventing extra scope or claiming completed evidence."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"document_information","work_product":"professional_report","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"private_detectives_investigators","sector":"retail_trade","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":4.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"Have an independent document reviewer inspect the rendered DOCX against the relational schedule rules, then have a domain-experienced reviewer judge operational usability, neutral scope, and the defensibility of the fallback. Reconcile disagreements by checking the artifact’s explicit labels and internal relationships rather than requiring a particular layout or exact dates.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["No supplied roster, exact branch names, travel map, or employee identities exist, so grading must accept role-level labels, synthetic internal IDs, and any internally consistent dates within the stated window.","The two defensible readings of the information-spread tension cannot be reduced to one exact sequence; the rubric therefore checks explicit, coherent choice and treatment rather than one answer key.","Page count and readability depend on the offline renderer, so geometry should be assessed on a standard office-suite rendering."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:14:02+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:14:02+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:14:02+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:14:02+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:14:02+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/be80d2db315aa944","declared_deliverables":["duncastle_interview_travel_sequence_plan.docx"]};
